IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `coa-definitions`

-- coa16-part19-general.l4: the Companies Act 2006, Part 19 (Debentures), "General provisions": ss 738 to 742
-- (lines 9669-9691 of ukpga-2006-46.txt).  Layer 1: the law, objectively, from the text alone.
--
-- SOURCE. A plain-text rendering of the Act from legislation.gov.uk made by a converter script; it is not the
-- official text and nothing here is "verified against the official text".  Every `-- src:` line is generated by
-- srcrefs.py from that file (work/build.py), never retyped.
--
-- HOW TO READ AN ANSWER (the rule of 2026-10-29, assumed, not ruled by a lawyer; NOTES.md says it again).
--   JUST TRUE   the text says the case is within the provision.
--   JUST FALSE  the text says no in its own words.  Each such branch carries
--               -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "<the quoted words>"
--   NOTHING     the text does not decide.  Each such branch carries -- NOTHING-kind (<why>), <why> being one of:
--               silent, list not closed, includes, undefined term, points outside the text, limited by its own wording.
--   A caller must never turn NOTHING into FALSE.  REFUSE is not used: "not covered" is NOTHING, asserted in the tests.
--
-- KEEL.  This module imports coa-definitions (which brings coa-core).  Every name here begins with the label of the
-- section it implements, as the naming rule says; the days of a period are counted in whole days on a clock that
-- starts at the day the period starts, so a #TRACE "AT 0" is the day of the event the period runs from.

-- =========================================================================================================
-- Part 19 -- Debentures: General provisions
-- =========================================================================================================

-- ---- s 738: Meaning of "debenture" ----------------------------------------------------------------------

-- src:9671 | 738 Meaning of “debenture”
-- src:9672 | In the Companies Acts“debenture” includes debenture stock, bonds and any other securities of a company, whether or not constituting a charge on the assets of the company.
@ref s 738 Meaning of "debenture" (src:9671-9672)
DECLARE `s 738 kind of instrument` IS ONE OF
    `s 738 debenture stock`
    `s 738 a bond`
    `s 738 another security of a company`
    `s 738 a share in a company`
    `s 738 something that is not a security of a company`

-- Plain gloss: "debenture" is a defined word of the Companies Acts that includes debenture stock, bonds and any other
-- securities of a company, whether or not they charge the company's assets.  The word "includes" leaves the list
-- open, so an instrument outside the list is "not covered", not "no".  The text does not say whether a share is
-- one of the "other securities" (s 755(5) treats "shares or debentures" as two things): fork F1.
@ref s 738 Meaning of "debenture" (src:9672)
GIVEN `the instrument` IS A `s 738 kind of instrument`
      `the instrument constitutes a charge on the assets of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the word is used in a provision of the Companies Acts (s 2(1))` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 738 the instrument is a debenture` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the word is used in a provision of the Companies Acts (s 2(1))`
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN
        -- whether or not the instrument constitutes a charge on the assets: the answer does not read that fact
        CONSIDER `the instrument`
        WHEN `s 738 debenture stock` THEN JUST TRUE
        WHEN `s 738 a bond` THEN JUST TRUE
        WHEN `s 738 another security of a company` THEN JUST TRUE
        WHEN `s 738 a share in a company` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (undefined term): the text does not say whether "any other securities of a company" reaches a share
        WHEN `s 738 something that is not a security of a company` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "includes debenture stock, bonds and any other securities of a company"
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "In the Companies Acts"
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the provision is one of the Companies Acts is s 2(1), taken as an input

-- ---- s 739: Perpetual debentures -------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- src:9673 | 739 Perpetual debentures
-- src:9674 | (1) A condition contained in debentures, or in a deed for securing debentures, is not invalid by reason only that the debentures are made—
-- src:9675 | (a) irredeemable, or
-- src:9676 | (b) redeemable only—
-- src:9677 | (i) on the happening of a contingency (however remote), or
-- src:9678 | (ii) on the expiration of a period (however long),
-- src:9679 | any rule of equity to the contrary notwithstanding.
-- src:9680 | (2) Subsection (1) applies to debentures whenever issued and to deeds whenever executed.
@ref s 739 Perpetual debentures (src:9673-9680)
GIVEN `the condition is contained in debentures, or in a deed for securing debentures` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the debentures are made irredeemable` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the debentures are made redeemable only on the happening of a contingency (however remote)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the debentures are made redeemable only on the expiration of a period (however long)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 739(1) the condition is invalid by reason only of how the debentures are made redeemable` MEANS
    IF NOT (`the condition is contained in debentures, or in a deed for securing debentures`)
    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A condition contained in debentures, or in a deed for securing debentures"
    ELSE IF       `the debentures are made irredeemable`
               OR `the debentures are made redeemable only on the happening of a contingency (however remote)`
               OR `the debentures are made redeemable only on the expiration of a period (however long)`
         THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "is not invalid by reason only that the debentures are made— (a) irredeemable, or (b) redeemable only— (i) on the happening of a contingency (however remote), or (ii) on the expiration of a period (however long), any rule of equity to the contrary notwithstanding"
         ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the text says nothing of a debenture redeemable in some other way

-- "Whenever issued": the answer does not read the date.
@ref s 739(2) Perpetual debentures: whenever issued (src:9680)
GIVEN `the date the debentures were issued or the deed was executed` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 739(2) subsection (1) applies to the debentures or deed` MEANS
    JUST TRUE -- the text: "Subsection (1) applies to debentures whenever issued and to deeds whenever executed"

-- ---- s 740: Enforcement of contract to subscribe for debentures ------------------------------------------

-- src:9681 | 740 Enforcement of contract to subscribe for debentures
-- src:9682 | A contract with a company to take up and pay for debentures of the company may be enforced by an order for specific performance.
@ref s 740 Enforcement of contract to subscribe for debentures (src:9681-9682)
GIVEN `the contract is with a company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the contract is to take up and pay for debentures of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 740 the contract may be enforced by an order for specific performance` MEANS
    IF `the contract is with a company` AND `the contract is to take up and pay for debentures of the company`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A contract with a company to take up and pay for debentures of the company"

-- ---- s 741: Registration of allotment of debentures -----------------------------------------------------

-- src:9683 | 741 Registration of allotment of debentures
-- src:9684 | (1) A company must register an allotment of debentures as soon as practicable and in any event within two months after the date of the allotment.
-- src:9685 | (2) If a company fails to comply with this section, an offence is committed by—
-- src:9686 | (a) the company, and
-- src:9687 | (b) every officer of the company who is in default.
-- src:9688 | (3) A person guilty of an offence under this section is liable on summary conviction to a fine not exceeding level 3 on the standard scale and, for continued contravention, a daily default fine not exceeding one-tenth of level 3 on the standard scale.
-- src:9689 | (4) For the duties of the company as to the issue of the debentures, or certificates of debenture stock, see Part 21 (certification and transfer of securities)
@ref s 741 Registration of allotment of debentures (src:9683-9689)
DECLARE `s 741 act` IS ONE OF
    `s 741 register the allotment of debentures`

-- "within two months after the date of the allotment": the last day is the corresponding date two months on, or the
-- last day of the shorter month when there is none (daydate's `add months` clamps: 31 December is 28 February in
-- 2023).  The deadline day itself is in time.  Fork F2.
@ref s 741(1) Registration of allotment of debentures: the period (src:9684)
GIVEN `the date of the allotment` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 741(1) the last day for registering the allotment` MEANS
    `add months` `the date of the allotment` 2

@ref s 741(1) Registration of allotment of debentures: the period in days (src:9684)
GIVEN `the date of the allotment` IS A DATE
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 741(1) the days allowed for registering the allotment` MEANS
    (Day (`s 741(1) the last day for registering the allotment` `the date of the allotment`)) MINUS (Day `the date of the allotment`)

-- Has the company done what s 741(1) requires?  "as soon as practicable" is a judgment the text hands to the facts
-- (a plain input); "in any event within two months after the date of the allotment" is a period the text fixes.
-- The company that has not registered while the two months have not run out has not yet failed: NOTHING.
@ref s 741(1) Registration of allotment of debentures (src:9684)
GIVEN `the date of the allotment` IS A DATE
      `the date the allotment was registered, if it has been` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `the allotment was registered as soon as practicable` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date now` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 741(1) the company has registered the allotment as the section requires` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the date the allotment was registered, if it has been`
    WHEN JUST registered THEN
        IF       registered AT MOST `s 741(1) the last day for registering the allotment` `the date of the allotment`
             AND `the allotment was registered as soon as practicable`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A company must register an allotment of debentures as soon as practicable and in any event within two months after the date of the allotment"
    WHEN NOTHING THEN
        IF `the date now` AT MOST `s 741(1) the last day for registering the allotment` `the date of the allotment`
        THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the two months have not run out and the allotment is not yet registered, so there is no answer yet
        ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "in any event within two months after the date of the allotment"

-- The duty as a regulative rule.  The clock counts days from the date of the allotment; "as soon as practicable" is
-- not a time the text fixes, so only the outer limit is modelled.
@ref s 741(1) Registration of allotment of debentures: the duty (src:9684)
GIVEN `the date of the allotment` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 741 act`
`s 741(1) the company must register the allotment` MEANS
    PARTY Company
    MUST `s 741 register the allotment of debentures`
    WITHIN `s 741(1) the days allowed for registering the allotment` `the date of the allotment`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY Company BECAUSE "s 741(1): the allotment of debentures was not registered within two months after the date of the allotment"

DECLARE `s 741(2) person` IS ONE OF
    `s 741(2) the company`
    `s 741(2) an officer of the company` HAS `s 741(2) the officer is in default (s 1121)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
    `s 741(2) another person`

-- "an offence is committed by (a) the company, and (b) every officer of the company who is in default."
-- The company's failure is read from s 741(1); an officer who is not "in default" is outside the class the text
-- names (a limit in its own wording), and whether an officer is in default is s 1121 (taken as an input).
@ref s 741(2) Registration of allotment of debentures: the offence (src:9685-9687)
GIVEN `the date of the allotment` IS A DATE
      `the date the allotment was registered, if it has been` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `the allotment was registered as soon as practicable` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date now` IS A DATE
      person IS A `s 741(2) person`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 741(2) the person commits an offence` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 741(1) the company has registered the allotment as the section requires` `the date of the allotment` `the date the allotment was registered, if it has been` `the allotment was registered as soon as practicable` `the date now`
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If a company fails to comply with this section, an offence is committed by"
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): whether the company has failed to comply is not yet known
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN
        CONSIDER person
        WHEN `s 741(2) the company` THEN JUST TRUE
        WHEN `s 741(2) an officer of the company` inDefault THEN
            CONSIDER inDefault
            WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
            WHEN JUST FALSE THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "every officer of the company who is in default"
            WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the officer is in default is s 1121
        WHEN `s 741(2) another person` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): the text names the company and its officers in default

-- "a fine not exceeding level 3 on the standard scale and, for continued contravention, a daily default fine not
-- exceeding one-tenth of level 3 on the standard scale."  The ceiling, never a tariff.
@ref s 741(3) Registration of allotment of debentures: the penalty (src:9688)
`s 741(3) the penalty for the offence` MEANS
    Penalty WITH
        `how convicted` IS `on summary conviction`
        `imprisonment not exceeding` IS NOTHING
        `fine not exceeding` IS JUST (`a fine not exceeding a level on the standard scale` 3 1)
        `daily default fine for continued contravention` IS JUST (`a fine not exceeding a level on the standard scale` 3 0.1)
        `imprisonment and fine together` IS FALSE

-- The pounds that a level on the standard scale or the statutory maximum stands for are not in the Act (inputs).
-- Used by the seat layer for every section whose penalty is a Fine limit.
@ref s 741(3) Registration of allotment of debentures: the penalty in pounds (src:9688)
GIVEN limit IS A `Fine limit`
      `the pounds that the level on the standard scale stands for` IS A NUMBER
      `the pounds that the statutory maximum stands for` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 741(3) the most that a fine limit allows, in pounds` MEANS
    CONSIDER limit
    WHEN `a fine without a stated limit` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): "a fine" with no ceiling stated
    WHEN `a fine not exceeding the statutory maximum` fraction THEN JUST (fraction TIMES `the pounds that the statutory maximum stands for`)
    WHEN `a fine not exceeding a level on the standard scale` level fraction THEN JUST (fraction TIMES `the pounds that the level on the standard scale stands for`)
    WHEN `a fine not exceeding an amount in pounds` pounds THEN JUST pounds

-- s 741(4) "For the duties of the company as to the issue of the debentures, or certificates of debenture stock, see
-- Part 21": a signpost, inert (reason 1), as the keel's fork F7 treats signposts; fork F3.

-- ---- s 742: Debentures to bearer (Scotland) -------------------------------------------------------------

-- src:9690 | 742 Debentures to bearer (Scotland)
-- src:9691 | Notwithstanding anything in the statute of the Scots Parliament of 1696, chapter 25, debentures to bearer issued in Scotland are valid and binding according to their terms.
@ref s 742 Debentures to bearer (Scotland) (src:9690-9691)
GIVEN `the debentures are debentures to bearer` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the debentures were issued in Scotland` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 742 the debentures are valid and binding according to their terms` MEANS
    IF `the debentures are debentures to bearer` AND `the debentures were issued in Scotland`
    THEN JUST TRUE -- notwithstanding anything in the statute of the Scots Parliament of 1696, chapter 25
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "debentures to bearer issued in Scotland"
